From d71ffbeb9138275f6b09d0ade5832cca79e89d74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Bodenham <matthew@bodenham.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:06:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] x1600-msc: unmapped backplane reads 0xffffffff (RAM-size walk
 fix)

The DHD's si_doattach RAM size walk scans the backplane word-by-word
from 0x0 (CMD53 fn1 word reads with per-32K-window CMD52 end reads)
and stops at the first nonzero word. With every non-chipcommon word
served as 0 the walk never terminated: it crossed the whole 512KB
SOCSRAM, kept going past the SI enum space and was still at 0x5f58000
after 280 s (the 'GCI/PMU poll' of the v0.68 traces is this walk).

Model the real decode: backplane windows in [0x80000, 0x18000000)
read 0xffffffff, on both the CMD53 path (before the chunk-cache
lookup - the 16-slot cache otherwise serves stale zero chunks and
lets the walk overrun to 0x88000, which si_doattach rejects) and on
the CMD52 fn1 word path used for the window-end reads.

With this the walk breaks at exactly 0x80000 (the 43430A1's 512KB
SOCSRAM) in ~1.1 s. si_doattach still rejects the attach afterwards;
that and the 512-byte CIS reads hanging in the soc_msc DMA path
(state:0, request never reaches the MSC; the model has no SoC DMAC)
are the next blockers - see M1 log v0.69.
---
 hw/mips/x1600.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/mips/x1600.c b/hw/mips/x1600.c
index 7022c15..5171d6d 100644
--- a/hw/mips/x1600.c
+++ b/hw/mips/x1600.c
@@ -508,6 +508,17 @@ static uint32_t x1600_msc_cmd52(X1600Msc *s, uint32_t arg)
             data |= (data & 0x10) ? 0x80 : 0;   /* HT_AVAIL */
             return data;
         }
+        if (!write && addr >= 0x8000) {
+            /* fn1 0x8000-0xffff is the 32K backplane window bank; word
+             * reads (bit15 set) fetch from the SBADDR-mapped backplane,
+             * same as the CMD53 path below. */
+            uint32_t sbaddr = s->fn1[0x1000a] | (s->fn1[0x1000b] << 8) |
+                              (s->fn1[0x1000c] << 16);
+            uint32_t bp = (sbaddr << 8) | (addr & 0x7fff);
+            if (bp >= 0x80000 && bp < 0x18000000) {
+                return 0xffffffffu;
+            }
+        }
         space = s->fn1 + addr;
     } else {
         return 0;
@@ -640,7 +651,18 @@ static void x1600_msc_command(X1600Msc *s)
                         }
                     }
                 }
-                if (chunk) {
+                if (bp >= 0x80000 && bp < 0x18000000) {
+                    /* Beyond the 43430A1's 512KB SOCSRAM banks and below
+                     * the SI enum space the backplane decodes to nothing
+                     * and the vendor core reads 0xffffffff there. The
+                     * DHD's RAM size walk in si_doattach scans the SRAM
+                     * word-by-word and stops at the first such word,
+                     * yielding the chip's 512KB RAM size; serving the
+                     * zero-filled chunk cache here instead let the walk
+                     * overrun to 0x88000 and si_doattach rejected the
+                     * result. The check must precede the chunk lookup. */
+                    memset(s->fifo, 0xff, c53cnt);
+                } else if (chunk) {
                     uint32_t off = bp & 0x7fff;
                     for (i = 0; i < c53cnt && off + i < 0x8000; i++) {
                         s->fifo[i] = chunk[off + i];
-- 
2.53.0

